WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:07.080
In a previous video, we started working 
on our new storage container.

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.680
We got the container just before the winter break.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.800
Then, we opened some space around it,
and finally we built a big roof on top.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:17.240
Now, it's time to start making the storage system.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.840
Welcome to a new Project Kamp update.

00:00:21.078 --> 00:00:22.920
One side will be our new material bank.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:26.960
To store offcuts to be used later,
and items that could have a second life.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.373
Such as windows or doors.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.307
The other side will hold our new waste system.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.542
We like the idea of not being a shame,
with the waste we generate.

00:00:35.542 --> 00:00:38.960
And, since our project is based on sustainability...

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.620
We also like to put the waste in the front.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:45.920
To, in the future, give a new value
to what now is considered garbage.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:49.600
But first, we need to do some landscaping
work around the container.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.920
For that, we will get a hand from the general help team.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:56.320
At the moment, I'm in the area that we cleared of last season.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.520
But, unfortunately, the brambles are already growing back...

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:04.280
The idea is to bring in humans, so that they step on the brambles,
 and the brambles stay away.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:07.800
But, to get the humans here, we need
to make the place a bit more comfortable.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:09.200
So, let's do that!

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.440
We try to remove the bass from the old mimosas.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:27.539
And, pull the new, sprouting ones.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.626
Okay, here we are trying a new strategy,

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:36.280
Putting the top of the mimosas on the bottom.

00:01:37.014 --> 00:01:42.520
To create like a barrier that gets the rainwater,
and retains it into the ground.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:46.080
So, all this soil that I'm standing on,
we got from leveling the container.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:49.080
Which, we can now use to put on top of the mimosa tops.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:18.200
So, here we have a strawberry tree, 
and we don't want people to step on it...

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:23.142
So, we are going to put this little sign here.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.840
- So beautiful!

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.840
It is beautiful!

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:38.880
We also always try to take care of 
the native species we find around.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:44.400
Here, next to the medronheiro, we have a nice open area!

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.560
We would like to create this
as a general help space.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:51.480
So, some chairs, a table and a flat levelled area could help.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.580
Okay, on three?

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:54.520
One...

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:55.719
Two...

00:02:56.159 --> 00:02:56.911
Three!

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.760
Thank you!

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:03.480
- Maybe we should bring our board in...

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:04.920
Oh, yeah! That's nice!

00:04:06.624 --> 00:04:09.024
- You take care of the cameras today!

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:30.972
Then, we cleared a circular area to be 
the new Human Hour space.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:38.613
And then, our journey to find useful uses to the mimosas,
this big bench was built.

00:04:50.226 --> 00:04:51.360
- It's a good two seater.

00:04:52.294 --> 00:04:55.294
You should have a little tub of tea and coffee here.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:09.720
To connect all these new places, 
we made multiple paths with the wood chips.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:49.264
Come on, people!

00:05:49.264 --> 00:05:50.766
Work! Work!

00:06:14.797 --> 00:06:19.054
To finish the job, we had to cut this mimosa,
that was almost falling onto the new roof.

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:40.552
- Now, the roof is safe!

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:47.520
Okay, so, the area has been transforming quite a bit!

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:48.679
Let's have a look!

00:06:50.147 --> 00:06:53.427
So, in the area, we have been taking quite a bit more of mimosas.

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:57.640
It's never bad to take out more, but then,
what do we do with all that material?

00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:01.560
We chopped it up in smaller pieces this time,
and lay it down on the waterlines.

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:06.120
This is to stop the water from sliding down,
but also help to decompose it faster.

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:08.640
With this little bridge, it becomes quite funny.

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:11.640
And, obviously, the native ones, they are highly cared.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:17.240
We also got the opportunity to create more neat meeting spaces.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:20.840
In this case, a new space for general help,
to have their Monday morning meeting.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:24.600
So, here we have a beautiful creation,
made out of mimosa.

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:26.542
You can have a look on the research module!

00:07:26.542 --> 00:07:29.280
This shapes the new Human Hour space.

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:31.320
Where we come together by the end of the week.

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:34.400
So, enough about this area.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:37.623
General Help did a great job, 
but we are going out towards the container.

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:43.800
We are going to start to build our material bank.

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:50.720
We have the roof ready, so we have a nice dry area 
around the container to start to store materials.

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:54.840
In this first material bank, 
we will store mainly wood in different sizes.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:59.194
Now, we try to standardize the sizes of the wood a bit,
that we use in the Kamp.

00:07:59.194 --> 00:08:03.468
In order to, in the future, be able to disassemble what we do.

00:08:03.468 --> 00:08:07.520
To reuse that wood, and like that,
expanding the life of the materials.

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:13.640
For this project, we have Eemeli, that will take care of the design, 
the building and the timing of the project.

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:14.983
If you want...

00:08:14.983 --> 00:08:15.976
- I can.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:22.280
First, I dug a trench, so we can have electricity in the container.

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:50.600
The power we use in the Kamp comes from the solar panels,

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:53.880
It's stored in batteries in the kitchen container.

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:59.160
Just like that, we have another building
connected to our off grid system.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:14.680
So, I'm going to start building the shelves,
that will make our storage system.

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:21.480
We wanted to design something that is strong,
 with common materials and to be easily replicated by others.

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:27.560
It will consist of materials that will be attached to the container wall.

00:10:28.077 --> 00:10:30.080
They will hold some arms. 

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:35.334
It will be adjustable, so it can be adapted
 to many different needs and materials.

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:52.680
I will start by doing the first piece,
to see if everything works.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:07.600
I was so nervous about the welding bottle, 
that I forgot to film it, but...

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:10.560
It seems to be fine!

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:13.560
Here is the result!

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:21.120
First one done!

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:24.200
Now, we need to do this times 24...

00:11:26.618 --> 00:11:27.495
Let's go!

00:11:27.495 --> 00:11:32.400
That's actually 23, because we have one.

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:42.200
Okay, cool!

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:45.120
Now, I have all the pieces, so I can start welding.

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:51.640
It will be a lot of welding, but I got new clothes, 
so I should be good to go...

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:53.529
And also, look!

00:12:54.740 --> 00:12:55.840
A good match.

00:12:57.644 --> 00:13:01.120
And the welding machine, it happens to be a Finnish brand.

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:04.200
So, that's even nicer!

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:36.739
All the arms are ready!

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:41.060
They can be sanded and painted!

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:45.000
But first, I need to work on the U-beams...

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:49.480
First, by cutting them, and then do a bunch of crazy stuff.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:23.000
So, this is how it goes...

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:27.480
The arm goes inside of the new beam.

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:33.240
And then, there's a hole and a bolt that holds everything together.

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:36.600
Next, we do a lot of holes...

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:41.120
Okay...

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:44.023
Now, I got all the U-beams drilled.

00:16:44.023 --> 00:16:52.720
The only thing is to drill the placement,
or where you attach it to the container.

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:56.600
It goes for each end one,
and maybe one in the middle.

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:58.000
I'm not sure yet...

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:01.000
Now, I'm going to mark their places.

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:43.898
Done!

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:48.720
Okay, the arms are ready to be painted next, but...

00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:52.640
I think somebody will help me with the painting.

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:54.640
Chester!

00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:56.943
Can you help me with the painting?

00:18:01.750 --> 00:18:02.686
No...

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:06.680
Timo, you want to do a little bit of sanding?

00:18:07.524 --> 00:18:09.240
- I have to go shopping...

00:18:09.240 --> 00:18:10.120
Sorry.

00:18:10.120 --> 00:18:11.880
I would love to, otherwise!

00:18:24.720 --> 00:18:28.480
They sanded and painted everything, to prevent rust.

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:36.811
I get used to say this, but the 40 x 40 x 3 millimeters U-beams,
 they have a good strength for our need!

00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:12.880
Now that all pieces are made, we can start assembling.

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:20.240
The container is not perfectly straight,
so we need to hit some of the bumps back.

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:24.200
To make it more even...

00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:27.853
- It seems that there is no other solution?

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:32.440
No, so, it's hammertime...

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:10.215
Without this one, it's awful!

00:20:10.215 --> 00:20:11.953
- What's happening here?

00:20:11.953 --> 00:20:13.784
But, it's pretty cool going inside!

00:20:13.784 --> 00:20:14.889
- What's happening here?

00:20:18.960 --> 00:20:20.880
This is a sound test.

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:21.440
- Yeah?

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:24.440
Okay, I'm ready!

00:20:39.488 --> 00:20:40.387
Do you see that?

00:20:40.387 --> 00:20:42.800
The area, where you hit with the hammer, is hotter!

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:45.440
Makes sense...

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:46.275
It's fun to see!

00:20:46.275 --> 00:20:47.350
Okay, wait a minute!

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:52.200
Here, I have a new thermal camera that we are trying,
but maybe Dave can talk more about it!

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:58.280
So, we got this thermal cam made by Topdon, 
and they send it to us, so we could try and showcase the features it has.

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:04.520
And, this thing, it gives you a high resolution infrared image 
on your phone screen, and it shows the temperature readings.

00:21:04.840 --> 00:21:07.760
You can tap on the image to get a point-temperature info.

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:10.126
You have this mode, where you can draw a line on the screen.

00:21:10.126 --> 00:21:13.263
It gives you the highest and the lowest temperature points on that line.

00:21:13.263 --> 00:21:17.527
You can also draw an area, and this will give you the hottest
and the coldest point in there.

00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:22.440
It has a wide range of temperature measurements,
from -20 to 500 degrees.

00:21:22.600 --> 00:21:27.040
Different settings to tailor the skill you're working with,
and the colors, and so on...

00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:32.560
We wanted to figure out what we could use it for,
 and we found a bunch of applications in Project Kamp.

00:21:32.560 --> 00:21:35.560
First, let's have a look at our cork insulation in the office.

00:21:35.760 --> 00:21:38.960
We found out some heat is leaking,
between the seams of the corkboard.

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:42.440
You can see the yellow lines more bright,
which means it's hotter.

00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:45.720
We also had a quick check
on our solar system.

00:21:45.720 --> 00:21:49.360
Good to see if some components overheat,
and therefore improve the layout of it.

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:52.546
Batteries are doing great and they're not overheating.

00:21:53.317 --> 00:21:56.797
Another cool application is also to see
if the compost pile is working.

00:21:56.920 --> 00:21:59.280
You can tell if it's hot enough inside there.

00:21:59.280 --> 00:22:01.760
Looks like it is, so no need to get our hands dirty.

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:07.680
And, as we're renovating old buildings, 
it's an interesting to see where the structure is weaker.

00:22:08.080 --> 00:22:11.400
For instance, those corners between
the ceiling and the wall get hotter.

00:22:11.800 --> 00:22:13.360
Which probably means there's less material.

00:22:13.360 --> 00:22:16.000
So, we might need to reinforce those areas.

00:22:16.000 --> 00:22:18.720
And, we couldn't avoid checking our recycled plastic roof.

00:22:18.720 --> 00:22:21.720
It's interesting to see the difference in temperature between the sheets.

00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:25.080
Probably because each panel
has a different plastic mix and color.

00:22:25.560 --> 00:22:27.640
So, we did a few quick tests with the camera.

00:22:27.640 --> 00:22:31.320
It seems like a useful tool and I can think of many other applications.

00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:37.400
So, one cool thing, you can also hook it up to your computer,
so that you can monitor the temperature over time.

00:22:37.400 --> 00:22:39.557
It would also be interesting to measure wildlife.

00:22:39.557 --> 00:22:43.000
And, maybe even at night, so that you can see
the heat patterns they leave.

00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:45.720
Maybe we can spot wildfires in the distance.

00:22:46.480 --> 00:22:50.720
What if you have like different colors of paint, 
and we can measure which one gets most hot?

00:22:50.720 --> 00:22:53.720
So, we can see what color we should paint our buildings.

00:22:53.760 --> 00:22:58.400
What we also like is that it's like not
an entire new device, but it's an add-on.

00:22:58.600 --> 00:23:01.600
It's a bit like Phonebloks,
like a module for your existing phone.

00:23:01.680 --> 00:23:05.560
Anyway, we'll continue to explore
more information in the link below.

00:23:05.960 --> 00:23:07.800
Let's continue with the container!

00:23:12.480 --> 00:23:15.102
Pretty good! Not bad!

00:23:16.129 --> 00:23:20.840
Now that the container is flat, let's install the system.

00:24:02.280 --> 00:24:04.680
After the first one was in place...

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:09.560
I did the same thing for the five other things, but I forgot to record it.

00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:11.045
So sorry...

00:24:11.045 --> 00:24:17.080
Actually, it took me a whole day to mount 
the six pins to the container.

00:24:17.400 --> 00:24:20.240
Since the container was so uneven...

00:24:20.240 --> 00:24:22.880
So, it's just a little bit more work than I was expecting.

00:24:23.761 --> 00:24:26.174
But now, it seems to be okay!

00:24:27.080 --> 00:24:32.160
It's kind of loose here, but...

00:24:33.000 --> 00:24:36.720
So, I need to add at a bolt to the middle.

00:24:50.960 --> 00:24:53.960
Now, I just have to put the arms in.

00:25:06.252 --> 00:25:07.251
- Good morning, Eemeli!

00:25:07.251 --> 00:25:08.640
Good morning.

00:25:08.640 --> 00:25:09.743
How does it look?

00:25:09.743 --> 00:25:11.183
- Good.

00:25:11.440 --> 00:25:13.680
How do you feel about it?

00:25:13.680 --> 00:25:15.040
- It's not bad!

00:25:15.040 --> 00:25:17.000
Could be worse, I think.

00:25:17.000 --> 00:25:18.360
- Well, always can be worse.

00:25:21.440 --> 00:25:22.880
Can I...?

00:25:24.840 --> 00:25:26.400
Is it strong enough for me?

00:25:26.400 --> 00:25:27.785
- I think so, yeah.

00:25:31.280 --> 00:25:32.640
Very strong!

00:25:32.640 --> 00:25:34.680
Now, I got the arms here.

00:25:34.680 --> 00:25:36.520
It looks nice!

00:25:36.520 --> 00:25:42.200
The only thing left to do is to bring all the wood here, 
but I need a few more hands for that...

00:25:42.320 --> 00:25:46.160
So, let's go and see, if there is any hands available!

00:25:47.800 --> 00:25:50.120
Okay, this is all the wood we need to move.

00:25:50.120 --> 00:25:53.760
There seems to be some happy people willing to help me!

00:25:57.920 --> 00:26:00.920
So, this wood needs to go there...

00:27:23.200 --> 00:27:28.840
Okay, one side is ready with our material bank,
and now we are going to jump to the other side!

00:27:28.840 --> 00:27:31.320
We are going to set up our first waste point.

00:27:31.320 --> 00:27:32.280
Eemeli is going to build it!

00:27:32.280 --> 00:27:35.311
It will have a similar structure done for the other side

00:27:35.311 --> 00:27:38.520
For this, we have Kevin that will start some research.

00:27:38.520 --> 00:27:43.400
To see the state where we are at,
to be able to set up our first waste system.

00:27:43.960 --> 00:27:47.240
Currently, we are using this recycling system.

00:27:47.640 --> 00:27:53.897
We have three colored bins, which is based on the waste system,
that applies to all of Portugal.

00:27:54.360 --> 00:27:57.880
The glass and paper are fairly understandable and very clear.

00:27:58.240 --> 00:28:04.080
But, there's a problem with the yellow one,
which makes a lot of different packaging material into one bin.

00:28:04.080 --> 00:28:13.560
For example, there are Tetra bags, plastic bags, 
hard plastic, and all kinds of metal mixed into one bin...

00:28:13.560 --> 00:28:17.480
So, it's difficult for people to understand and to do it properly.

00:28:17.600 --> 00:28:22.880
We want to do a more detail separation on the yellow bin,
and we have done some testing.

00:28:22.960 --> 00:28:25.960
So, let me show you.

00:28:35.880 --> 00:28:38.800
Okay, so, this is what we have now!

00:28:38.800 --> 00:28:41.349
You can see a lot of different materials mixed together...

00:28:41.349 --> 00:28:47.880
With barbed wire, metal, dangerous stuff, 
are all together here and it's very messy...

00:28:48.120 --> 00:28:52.840
Either, you come to recycle, or you want to rescue
some of the material for your project.

00:28:52.840 --> 00:28:54.840
So, I think we can do better than this.

00:28:54.840 --> 00:28:56.360
Let me show you!

00:28:59.960 --> 00:29:05.800
Okay, so, this is where Eemeli will be building
the new recycling system shelving.

00:29:06.200 --> 00:29:11.370
We want to separate all kinds of material 
into a more tidy rack.

00:29:11.370 --> 00:29:16.797
So, people can recover the material more easily,
and also separate them more easily.

00:29:16.960 --> 00:29:21.645
It's also very easy to load it onto a truck, 
and send it to a recycling point.

00:29:21.645 --> 00:29:29.080
To decide that, we also have been doing a waste audit 
to count what kind of waste we're actually producing.

00:29:29.480 --> 00:29:30.840
I can show you that as well.

00:29:49.800 --> 00:29:55.800
So, we have stockpiled all the recyclables, 
and separated them into a clear system.

00:29:56.240 --> 00:29:59.240
To see what kind of material we actually got.

00:29:59.520 --> 00:30:06.480
Like, for example, there's a lot of metal, coffee bags,
 and Tetra bags and also a lot of plastic bags...

00:30:06.760 --> 00:30:12.421
So, these are materials we can potentially 
reuse here locally for our future project.

00:30:12.421 --> 00:30:19.000
Or, we can stop hauling more enough 
to find a trustable recycler to send it directly to them.

00:30:19.280 --> 00:30:24.764
In case anyone is wondering why we only have 
the top and the bottom part of the can...

00:30:24.764 --> 00:30:28.188
It's because we have been using the size for another project.

00:30:28.188 --> 00:30:31.560
So, we want to make some signs
for the recycling system.

00:30:31.920 --> 00:30:35.440
But, the sign will placed outdoors,
so we need it to be weatherproof...

00:30:35.760 --> 00:30:37.770
Let's see if we can make a sign out of it!

00:31:09.640 --> 00:31:14.000
Now, the piece of wood is covered,
with the aluminum from the beer can.

00:31:14.000 --> 00:31:17.311
So, now, we try to write the sign on it.

00:31:42.000 --> 00:31:46.520
This is how it will look like,
and I'm quite happy about it.

00:31:46.720 --> 00:31:49.560
So, let's make three more of them!

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:01.400
We have made the signs!

00:32:01.920 --> 00:32:04.920
Let's put this onto the crates!

00:32:47.760 --> 00:32:49.640
800 grams.

00:32:49.640 --> 00:32:54.240
So, after the audit, we decided
to keep the glass and paper bin...

00:32:54.240 --> 00:32:57.600
Because, it is more or less a more straight forward separation.

00:32:58.000 --> 00:33:02.880
And, for the yellow bin, we want to do
a more detailed one, which is four categories.

00:33:03.360 --> 00:33:09.666
One is Precious Plastic, where we keep the PPE
 and HDPE, for a future project.

00:33:09.666 --> 00:33:16.917
And then, the soft plastic, which is mainly the plastic bags, 
the chip bags and the Tetra bags.

00:33:16.917 --> 00:33:21.441
Which we can compress and save space,
and also, maybe for future projects.

00:33:21.918 --> 00:33:26.720
And, hard plastic, which is really the plastic
that we have no idea on how to use...

00:33:26.960 --> 00:33:29.960
But still, we want to put it into a tidy way

00:33:30.200 --> 00:33:32.840
Metal is the more valuable one.

00:33:32.840 --> 00:33:35.920
We separate them into aluminum,
and mixed-in metal.

00:33:35.920 --> 00:33:39.200
We would be stockpiling them into a more bigger quantity.

00:33:39.240 --> 00:33:44.727
Either, we send it to a trustful recycler,
 or we can reuse them locally here.

00:33:44.727 --> 00:33:50.480
We will keep doing research, and see how it goes,
and it will evolve and it depends how it goes...

00:33:50.680 --> 00:33:52.320
We will keep improving it.

00:33:52.320 --> 00:33:55.320
This is our first version of the recycling system!

00:33:55.440 --> 00:33:56.520
All the bins are ready!

00:33:56.520 --> 00:33:59.160
When the shelves are done, we can start installing them.

00:34:44.590 --> 00:34:49.320
Here are some welds brought onto the container.

00:34:49.320 --> 00:34:54.469
So, there is a weld seam that needs to be smoothened out...

00:35:18.200 --> 00:35:22.000
This is a good example what the video makers actually do...

00:35:22.640 --> 00:35:26.560
They just vandalize all the things we have.

00:35:29.160 --> 00:35:32.865
Now that the beams are there, I can put the arms on!

00:35:55.160 --> 00:35:57.440
- By the way, don't forget to subscribe!

00:35:57.440 --> 00:35:58.972
♡ Thank you! ♡

00:36:01.320 --> 00:36:03.440
The arms are all in place!

00:36:03.440 --> 00:36:06.040
Now, it's time to make some wood supports.

00:37:00.160 --> 00:37:03.720
Now, I need to make two more shelves.

00:37:04.320 --> 00:37:06.480
So, three in total.

00:37:06.480 --> 00:37:07.803
It's loud in here...

00:37:08.464 --> 00:37:14.640
The fact that this place feels quiet and silent,
and everything is in balance in reality...w

00:37:14.640 --> 00:37:17.960
So, almost all of the day is very noisy.

00:37:19.400 --> 00:37:21.120
They just don't show it to you!

00:37:41.280 --> 00:37:43.240
This is flexing quite a lot...

00:37:43.240 --> 00:37:48.240
So, I want to add one more arm in the middle.

00:38:05.160 --> 00:38:06.160
Better!

00:38:08.435 --> 00:38:11.435
I broke it already...

00:39:07.920 --> 00:39:10.920
This also works for naps.

00:39:23.000 --> 00:39:28.360
Just some hours after we finished, it started to rain, 
so we could put our storage system to the test!

00:39:33.320 --> 00:39:36.320
- Are you dry?

00:39:41.680 --> 00:39:43.600
I think we're good, but let's see...

00:39:43.600 --> 00:39:45.316
Time will tell.

00:39:48.880 --> 00:39:51.240
This is the system that we created.

00:39:51.240 --> 00:39:55.280
So, it consists of six beams,
and six beams on each side.

00:39:55.280 --> 00:39:58.935
The same system on both sides of the container,

00:39:58.935 --> 00:40:03.863
We have seven holes, and into those holes,
you can put the arms.

00:40:03.863 --> 00:40:07.803
You can mount the arm, by putting the bolt through.

00:40:09.240 --> 00:40:13.360
The beams are bolted straight to the container.

00:40:13.360 --> 00:40:17.680
So, we wanted to make a system,
that is simple enough to make here.

00:40:18.320 --> 00:40:21.920
And maybe, simple enough to replicate also!

00:40:23.011 --> 00:40:32.285
The materials that we used are standard sizes,
so it should be available everywhere you can get metal!

00:40:35.080 --> 00:40:37.960
So, this is the waste side of the storage.

00:40:39.720 --> 00:40:42.680
We have put the windows here from the white tent.

00:40:42.680 --> 00:40:49.080
And also, on top, we put some things
 that we don't need that often...

00:40:49.080 --> 00:40:54.000
Also, some cocoa, gas, beer, and some crates...

00:40:54.588 --> 00:40:57.084
We use them a lot!

00:40:59.200 --> 00:41:02.200
And also, the spiky wire.

00:41:04.560 --> 00:41:08.240
At some point, we probably will add some more shelves here.

00:41:08.480 --> 00:41:13.920
I guess we just have a lot of stuff,
and this is a good dry place to store stuff.

00:41:14.764 --> 00:41:18.257
It's good to have a system that is changeable!

00:41:23.920 --> 00:41:28.760
The material bank is a nice upgrade, 
because we can start stocking ahead of time for our projects.

00:41:28.960 --> 00:41:35.600
That will reduce delays and most importantly, 
we can start to store many materials we want to reuse properly.

00:41:35.720 --> 00:41:39.000
For the waste system, we are still in early stages of our research.

00:41:39.280 --> 00:41:41.760
But, there is enough improvement for the moment!

00:41:41.760 --> 00:41:44.400
Now, it's easier to load and unload the bins.

00:41:44.400 --> 00:41:47.280
We can align better with the local recycling facilities.

00:41:47.280 --> 00:41:50.509
We can even think better of how to reuse and upcycle!

00:41:51.170 --> 00:41:56.080
In the next update, we will continue clearing the mimosas 
around Basekamp to improve our fire resilience.

00:41:56.400 --> 00:41:59.040
We will do some testing and a bit of research.

00:41:59.040 --> 00:42:03.563
Now that the outside of the container is ready,
we also have created this area around.

00:42:03.563 --> 00:42:07.240
Where we can sit chill, or just enjoy the shade.

